NAME
    tmux - manage multiple independent shell sessions

SYNOPSIS
    tmux new [name]
    tmux list
    tmux switch <name>
    tmux kill <name>

DESCRIPTION
    Creates, lists, switches between, and destroys independent shell
    sessions within a single DianaSh instance when the host enables
    session management. Each session maintains its own variables,
    command history, last exit status ($?), pending multi-line input,
    and active account, while sharing the same underlying host and
    attached emulator state.

    A new session inherits the current session's active account and
    service bindings. Session names and accounts are preserved across
    host session resets.

OPTIONS
    new [name]
        Create a session (auto-named session-1, session-2, ... if name
        is omitted) and switch to it.
    list
        List all sessions, marking the active session with '*'.
    switch <name>
        Switch to an existing session.
    kill <name>
        Destroy an existing session. Fails if <name> is the only
        remaining session. Killing the active session switches to a
        remaining session.

EXAMPLES
    tmux new
    tmux new investigation
    tmux list
    tmux switch investigation
    tmux kill session-1

EXIT STATUS
    0   Subcommand completed (or usage printed for missing arguments).
    1   Session management is disabled, duplicate name on new, unknown
        session name, or attempt to kill the last remaining session.

SEE ALSO
    ps(1), kill(1), who(1), su(1), dianash(1)
